.TH IO_PREFETCH 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
iob_prefetch \- Prefetch data into the I/O batch buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/iob_internal.h>

.IB void
.IB iob_prefetch(
.IB io_batch* b,
.IB uint64 bytes
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBiob_prefetch\fR function prefetches data into the I/O batch buffer. This function is used to optimize the performance of I/O operations by loading data into the cache in advance.

The function takes the following parameters:

.IB b
Pointer to the I/O batch buffer.

.IB bytes
Number of bytes to prefetch.

The function does not return any value.

The function is part of the \fBiob\fR library, which provides a framework for managing I/O operations in batch mode.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBiob_prefetch\fR function to prefetch data into the I/O batch buffer:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/iob.h>

int main() {
  io_batch* batch = iob_new(100); // Hint for 100 entries
  if (!batch) {
    perror("iob_new");
    return 1;
  }

  // Add data to the batch buffer
  iob_adds(batch, "Hello, World!");
  iob_adds(batch, "This is a test.");

  // Prefetch data into the batch buffer
  iob_prefetch(batch, 1024); // Prefetch 1024 bytes

  // Process the batch buffer
  while (iob_bytesleft(batch) > 0) {
    iob_execute(batch);
  }

  // Free the I/O batch buffer
  iob_free(batch);

  printf("I/O batch buffer created, prefetched, processed, and freed\n");

  return 0;
}
.nef